+// Issue #681 (slice 4b of 7 of the #635 re-slicing, 0016 decision 7(e)): **the three maintenance
+// passes that walk the committed namespace themselves — reconstruction, backfill, rebalance —
+// resolve every committed object the way every other consumer resolves one, contain per object what
+// they cannot read, and refuse (rather than abort or silently discard) the work this slice does not
+// own.** On the base all three read the chunk map inline out of the record
+// (`chunk_map.as_flat().ok_or(SegmentedMapUnsupported)?`, seven sites), so ONE segmented object
+// turns repair, fill and drain into an `Err` for EVERY object in the store.
+//
+// Six legs, each driving ALL THREE passes over ONE store — one test per property; the pinned
+// decisions ride as sub-assertions. **No assertion names a symbol this patch introduces**: the red
+// leg reverts production, so one would fail to COMPILE instead of failing an assertion.
+
+#![forbid(unsafe_code)]
+
+use std::collections::{BTreeMap, HashMap};
+use std::sync::{Arc, Mutex};
+
+use async_trait::async_trait;
+use bytes::Bytes;
+use tracing::instrument::WithSubscriber;
+use tracing_subscriber::prelude::*;
+use wyrd_coordination_mem::MemCoordination;
